    "divergence_note": "All fifteen rows agree, on the first run. That is recorded rather than celebrated: this is a rule written the same day in three languages by the same author, so agreement says the three implementations match each other, not that the rule is right. What the rows establish is narrower and checkable. The same four kinds, the older kindless shape and a null kind are all recognised; the decoded size comes out identical, including for padded, malformed and line-wrapped base64; and nothing that is not a media shape is rewritten. Rows med-0012, med-0013 and med-0014 are LIMITS, pinned so no language quietly widens its own rule: bytes under an unknown or homoglyph kind, or pasted into a prompt as text, are exported in all three."
